            <h3>Overview of Train Duration, Distance, and Travel Time</h3>

            <p>The train from Chicago to Seattle is a long, comfortable ride with lots of time to sightsee on the way. This train route is roughly 3,000 kilometers (1,860 miles) long and offers many options, including the faster Coast Starlight or the slower Empire Builder.</p>


            <h2>Train Duration by Type</h2>

            <p>Travel time from Chicago to Seattle by train varies depending on the service you choose. Amtrak offers a variety of train types with varying maximum speeds. For example, the same route on the Coast Starlight runs faster and therefore in a shorter time window than on the more scenic Empire Builder.</p>


