            <h3>High-Speed vs Regional Trains</h3>

            <p>High-speed rail and regional choices on this route are run by Amtrak. The Coast Starlight is actually a middle-speed train, which means it lets you travel the farthest in the least amount of stops possible (similar to an express train), while the Empire Builder is slower and takes many scenic stops.</p>


            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>

            <p>Developing a travel strategy- your preference between HSTs–High Speed Trains and regional trains, can make or break how well your total fares accompany each aspect of travel. The creation of high-speed rail lines like the Coast Starlight is ideal for travelers who want to arrive at their destination as quickly and efficiently as possible. However, if you are okay with a slower pace and want more opportunities for exteriors, then the Empire Builder.</p>


