            <h2>Train vs Bus vs Flight Comparison</h2>
            <p>When planning your journey from Chicago to Seattle, it’s important to compare all available transportation options. While trains are the most popular choice for this route, buses and flights are also alternatives depending on your preferences for time, comfort, and budget.</p>

            <h3>Train</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Duration:</b> Approximately 35-40 hours</li>
                <li><b>Comfort:</b> High (spacious seating, dining options, scenic views)</li>
                <li><b>Flexibility:</b> High (multiple train times available)</li>
                <li><b>Convenience:</b> Moderate (stations are well-connected to local transport)</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Bus</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Duration:</b>  Approximately 48-50 hours</li>
                <li><b>Comfort:</b>  Medium (less legroom, fewer amenities)</li>
                <li><b>Flexibility:</b>  Low (fewer departures, fixed schedules)</li>
                <li><b>Convenience:</b>  Low (longer travel time and fewer amenities)</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Flight</h3>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Duration:</b> Approximately 4.5-5 hours</li>
                <li><b>Comfort: </b>Low (airport security, seating, and limited legroom)</li>
                <li><b>Flexibility:</b> High (numerous flights available daily)</li>
                <li><b>Convenience:</b> Low (airport procedures and longer travel time when considering the entire process)</li>
